{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791536665,"nonce":"HTjXQq4AjU3nTIkKod7ThitaV84=","message":"Isolated the remaining function ABI mismatch in TestCasts without its sibling module dependencies. /tmp/DynamicFunctionAbiProbe.hx returns a Float-\u003eFloat function through a Dynamic formal/result, assigns it to Int-\u003eFloat, and calls it with 123. Native Haxe prints converted=123.25; Rayzor prints converted=0.25. Evidence: /tmp/rayzor-dynamic-function-abi-native.log and /tmp/rayzor-dynamic-function-abi-before.log.\n\nThe compiler already generates ensure_varargs_typed_adapter for a Dynamic-to-function conversion; it boxes typed arguments, calls haxe_call_method_dynamic and unwraps the declared result. Runtime haxe_closure_typed_view selects that adapter only for varargs closures and passes ordinary closures through unchanged, leaving the caller and original callee with different numeric ABIs. No fix applied yet. Typed views also need to preserve closure identity. TestCasts separately needs sibling subtype module loading (MyClass.CI1 under package unit) before its interface checks can pass.","files":null}]}